      "title": "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "84ecd2c3-a963-51d4-8ce9-6888022191bb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2(x-8)}{3{y}^{2}}.$ Assume $x-8>0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(x-8)}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x-8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2(x-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2(x-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={(x-8)}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={(x-8)}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{(x-8)}^{2}+C}.\n$$\n\nUse the real cube root, on intervals where $y\\ne 0.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1fd7b13c-755f-5711-9d4f-8b0101057598",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "1b52b4c6-0ef2-5035-a331-753cce38d3cd",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + \\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}"
            },
